{
 "summary": "Checkout fails with gateway 502s because orders returns 504 after timing out on inventory POST /reserve. Sampled traces put most self time in inventory (release 3.1.5), whose p95 reached 4.77s while returning no 5xx. Orders was deployed 2.7.0 -> 2.8.4 about 32s before the first errors. That deploy is a strong lead, but the evidence does not show why inventory slowed or whether the deploy caused it.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory POST /reserve became slow, with p95 up to 4.77s and about 2.4s of self time in sampled traces. Orders times out waiting on it (about 2s), returns 504, and gateway reports 502 on POST /checkout. Why inventory slowed is not established. The orders 2.8.4 deploy at 09:19:13Z immediately preceded the symptoms and may have contributed, for example through a changed timeout or call pattern, but no evidence directly links them.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-e2e39db8ac21",
   "ev-26c19de1a5b9",
   "ev-656c8b55f38b",
   "ev-dabccf61a069",
   "ev-9c256a29fb9f"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders was deployed 2.7.0 -> 2.8.4 at 09:19:13Z. The first 'timed out reserving inventory' errors appeared 32s later, at 09:19:45Z.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a4e6073d5623",
    "ev-656c8b55f38b"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders gives up after about 2s: failing checkout traces last 2.01-2.04s, while inventory self time in those traces averages about 2.4-2.55s. Inventory keeps working after its caller has already timed out.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e2e39db8ac21"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders 5xx ratio reached 100% and gateway's reached 68.5% by the end of the window, so the failure is worsening.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-dabccf61a069",
    "ev-3844baeb62e1"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:19:13Z",
   "event": "Orders deployed 2.7.0 -> 2.8.4 by ci-pipeline",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a4e6073d5623"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:19:45Z",
   "event": "Orders starts logging 'timed out reserving inventory'; gateway starts logging 'checkout failed: orders returned 504'",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-656c8b55f38b",
    "ev-9c256a29fb9f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:20:13Z",
   "event": "p95 latency crosses 1s on inventory, orders and gateway; 5xx ratio crosses 5% on orders and gateway",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-26c19de1a5b9",
    "ev-dabccf61a069",
    "ev-3844baeb62e1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:21:55Z",
   "event": "All 20 sampled error traces show gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e2e39db8ac21"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:22:13Z",
   "event": "Last gateway checkout error logged (206 total); orders 5xx ratio at 100%",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-9c256a29fb9f",
    "ev-dabccf61a069"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway as the origin: it only relays orders' 504 as a 502, and its trace self time is not dominant.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e2e39db8ac21",
    "ev-9c256a29fb9f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory returning errors: its 5xx ratio stayed at 0%. The failure mode is latency, not inventory errors.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-26c19de1a5b9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A large traffic surge: gateway request rate stayed around 2 rps (avg 1.97, max 2.34), and inventory request rate (avg 1.35) matches orders, with no sign of call amplification.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-3844baeb62e1",
    "ev-26c19de1a5b9",
    "ev-dabccf61a069"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Why inventory /reserve slowed. There are no inventory logs, resource or saturation metrics, or database or dependency evidence.",
  "Whether inventory 3.1.5 was recently deployed. No inventory deployment record is in the snapshot.",
  "What changed in orders 2.8.4, such as the client timeout for inventory, reservation request size or pattern, or retries. A diff or config change is needed to confirm or reject a causal link.",
  "Inventory latency before 09:19:13Z, which would show whether inventory was already slow and the deploy only lowered the orders timeout.",
  "Whether trace self-time attribution is precise. Inventory self time (about 2.4s) exceeds root trace duration (about 2.0s), which suggests the inventory span outlives the caller's timeout."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back orders to 2.7.0 and watch whether orders and gateway 5xx ratios and inventory p95 recover.",
   "rationale": "The deploy immediately preceded the symptoms and rollback is low-risk. Recovery would confirm the link; no recovery points at inventory itself.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a4e6073d5623",
    "ev-656c8b55f38b",
    "ev-dabccf61a069"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Investigate inventory POST /reserve: check its logs, CPU and memory, DB and lock contention, and any recent inventory changes.",
   "rationale": "Trace self time shows inventory is where the time is spent, and its p95 latency reached 4.77s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e2e39db8ac21",
    "ev-26c19de1a5b9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Diff orders 2.7.0 vs 2.8.4, focusing on the inventory client timeout, reservation payloads and retry behavior.",
   "rationale": "This would establish whether the deploy changed how orders calls inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a4e6073d5623",
    "ev-e2e39db8ac21"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
